  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballymena Urban Council, January 1929. Market Ward was uncontested after Mr. William Cameron's withdrawal; Town Hall and Harryville Ward were contested. 1,290 of 1,600 voters polled (80.6 per cent); 10 spoiled papers. Shaw was chairman of the council."
